      "type": "summary",
      "text": "### Transaction Analysis\n\n**1. Basic Tier Purchase (Success)**\n*   **Payment & Escrow:** The transaction initiated a deposit of **10,000** units (representing the 0.01 test USDC basic deposit) into the native NEAR vault. This acts as an escrow, not a direct payment to the provider.\n*   **Reuse & Execution:** The session (`sessionId: 1a8e62f8-basic`) successfully processed **10 requests**. This demonstrates the time-based stream reuse capability where multiple API calls are covered under a single deposit window.\n*   **Refund & Earnings:** Upon the explicitly injected outage causing closure:\n    *   **Earned Tokens:** **20** units were marked as `claimable` for the provider based on actual usage.\n    *   **Refund:** The remaining **9,980** units were automatically returned to the vault (`refundedToVault`), ensuring no funds were lost due to the premature termination.\n*   **Verification:**\n    *   Open Transaction: `C2e8cqYYYuCBC9yymCoMwp6awpsCmceWpZ7s34NcDoSm`\n    *   Close Transaction: `BqQm62i1ZDz8hn1xYFBAXPjN7BYBBdHfp6qA6K2VxGdd`\n\n**2. Premium Tier Attempt (Denial)**\n*   **Result:** The request for the premium tier was **DENIED**.\n*   **Reason:** The deterministic policy worker returned `RATE_LIMIT`. Despite the basic session completing, the system enforced a restriction preventing the upgrade or parallel execution of the premium tier, adhering to the requirement that \"Premium must be denied.\"\n\n**Summary of Observations**\nThe system correctly handled the lifecycle of a test token deposit: locking funds in escrow, tracking usage via a reusable stream, calculating provider earnings versus user refunds upon forced closure, and strictly enforcing access policies by denying the premium tier request. No production decentralization or Chainlink execution was claimed; all operations occurred within the defined NEAR test environment constraints.",
